Z||000003||dman||01-26-2001||04:39 PM||||Hello.<P>David has been extremely busy and has difficulty responding to his email queries. He's not someone like the Fiero Store or Kick Hill with full time resources dedicated to selling fiero parts. Its just one guy.<P>His URL says it all, <A HREF="http://www.usedfieroparts.com." TARGET=_blank>www.usedfieroparts.com.</A>  He carries used fiero parts, and he sells them for -very- fair prices. These are good used pieces, he never sells junk, and he's <BR>good about describing the true quality of the pieces he sells. The ones that are rough and need work are described exactly as that, and its reflected in the reduced price for those pieces (he'll sometimes put on a clearance sale for such pieces). While the ones that are in prime shape are sold for very fair prices. Compare the prices with other used fiero parts suppliers and you'll see exactly what I mean.<P>The way I see it is if he has a part that you need, and you like the price, send him an email. If he responds then its all good. If he doesn't then buy elsewhere. <P>Personally, I'm thrilled that someone like him takes the time to sell his spare parts at such good prices (instead of placing them on ebay and trying to get the most money). Too bad he takes so long to respond to his email.<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000004||Haze_Performance||01-26-2001||07:28 PM||||Ive <B>never</B> bad mouthed any Fiero Parts Vender, But this is ridiculous<P> <B><BR>David has been extremely busy and has difficulty responding to his email queries. He's not someone like the Fiero Store or Kick Hill with full time resources dedicated to selling fiero parts. Its just one guy.</B><P>Then Maybe the webite shouldnt be setup like its a Fiero business.. <P><B>The way I see it is if he has a part that you need, and you like the price, send him an email. If he responds then its all good. If he doesn't then buy elsewhere.</B><P>What the hell is that about? I was looking for more info about the dash thats on the site.. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.cyberverse.com/~cyco/fieroparts/rpa/rpaint.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cyberverse.com/~cyco/fieroparts/rpa/rpaint.htm</A>  <P>Busy or not..Maybe he shound be a bit more professional.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ws6fierobanner.gif"> <BR><B>"AHHHHH!!!!!!!!!!! All Fiero's don't start on fire you BONEHEAD!!!!"</B>||||reg||8
Z||000005||dman||01-26-2001||11:28 PM||||Hi Carl. I got the impression that you were a little perturbed with my previous reply. Of course I could be mistaken...and if I am then please disregard what I'm about to say.<P>The purpose of my reply was to inform you and anyone else reading this post that although David (www.usedfieroparts.com) is often difficult to contact when it comes to email, he sells some very nice used fiero parts at a good price (he even sells some brand new fiero related accessories for a good price too).<P>Here's how I see it. Lets say you're walking down the street and discover this Auto parts store with some great window displays. You can see all kinds of stuff through the windows that you are interested in. You walk up to the door, knock, and the store owner opens the door and lets you in. You then ask, "Hey, I'd like that GT Wing thats on display". If the store owner then turned his back to you and walked away without a word, well....I'd think you'd get upset (I know I sure would!).<P>Let me pose another scenario. While walking down the street you see this cool store. You go up to the front door and knock. Nobody answers. You knock again, still no answer. Ah heck, you wait a week and knock on that door again. Still no answer!!! You go to the store next door and ask, "Anyone know how to get ahold of...".<P>Well, I think what I described is close to what's happening. Instead of a physical building, with store front windows, you discovered a website that described used fiero parts for sale.<P>Yeah, I agree. It stinks that no one is answering that door. One point I want to make is that you have the choice to keep walking until you find another store with cool stuff. Maybe that other store will have even better stuff, or at better prices. The key point is that it is -your- choice. And choices are good.<P>So while David may not be the greatest at responding to email, I'm glad he's around. Incidentally there are other folks like David, cool people who also provide useful fiero parts or accessories. One person in particular has some really cool stuff, short shifters, recessed headlights. He's so busy right now that he too is not able to answer every email that comes his way, but no one is outright saying that he shouldn't setup his webpage like its a business. You can't always get what you want, that's life. Although I sure would like to get a pair of those headlights!<P>I guess the point I'm trying to make is that even though the store front door doesn't always open whenever you come knocking, when it finally does open you know you're going to get a good product at a fair price.<P>I'm sorry that you aren't getting replies to your email. I'll be frank with you, I never email David. I call him by phone, that way I get an immediate response. I know his phone number because I've done business with him in the past (and will be purchasing more items in the future). Being that you are a fellow forum member I'm inclined to just give you his number. But that really wouldn't be appropriate. But I can call him up and tell him to check his email, in particular to look for an email from "fiero@carcollector.net". If you are still interested would you like me to do that? I mean this with all sincerity, I'm just another fiero forum member trying to help out.<P>Cheers, dman.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Haze_Performance||01-26-2001||11:57 PM||||Hi dman,<BR>  I was in no way directing my comments toward you. I'm sorry if it sounded that way. I was just venting my frustration of not getting my email's replied to. You see I'm in dire need of a dash or cover. I really wanted to get the info about the one on his site. I have to replace my dash ASAP and I just needed to know the info before I can make the decision (Look for a used stock one or buy his) Sorry if I came off like an A** H***.. Any help you can give me would be greatly appreciated.    <P><BR>TIA  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Carl<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ws6fierobanner.gif"> <BR><B>"AHHHHH!!!!!!!!!!! All Fiero's don't start on fire you BONEHEAD!!!!"</B>||||reg||11
